+### 8. Ticket CLI and project
+
+Slices become vault tickets, so the Obsidian ticket CLI and a project must exist.
+
+```bash
+TICKET_CLI=${TICKET_CLI:-<vault>/_system/bin/ticket}
+test -x "$TICKET_CLI" || echo "BLOCKED: ticket CLI not found"
+```
+
+Resolve `TICKET_PROJECT` from `projects-index.yaml` (the project whose `repos` contain the git root of
+the plan's repository). If no project matches, stop and ask the human. Do not guess a project.
+Resolve `GH_REPO` from `git remote get-url origin`. On a fork, always pass `--repo <origin owner>/<repo>`
+to `gh`, never the upstream.
+
